WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:04.810
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

00:04.810 --> 00:12.530
Asano hitogomi o nagamete coffee nondeiru
Watching a crowd in the morning, and drinking coffee

00:13.490 --> 00:21.500
Aseri nado naikano youni hitoni wa mieru daro
People must see me as if I don't have any worries

00:22.120 --> 00:29.960
lma menomae ni atomodori dekinai jikan ga
I know that the time I will never be able to get back

00:30.750 --> 00:38.260
Tashika ni nagareteru koto o watashi wa shitteru
Is moving in front of me

00:38.470 --> 00:47.480
Marude kyou shika nai toiu ikikata o shitemita toki
If I live like today is the last day of my life

00:47.770 --> 00:55.530
Saisho ni nani ga mieru darou
I wonder what I can see first

00:56.610 --> 01:00.870
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:01.290 --> 01:09.290
Sore ga donnani chiisana hikari demo ii
I don't care no matter how small the light is

01:09.790 --> 01:11.800
Sugata o misete hoshii
I just wish to see its shape

01:11.800 --> 01:16.010
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:16.680 --> 01:22.430
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.430 --> 01:22.720
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.720 --> 01:29.190
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Sonna hito ni deaitai
Who I can tell my honest feelings to

01:29.190 --> 01:31.020
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology

01:39.280 --> 01:40.210
<i>Dad!</i>

01:41.950 --> 01:44.220
<i>He still seems to be</i>
<i>holding onto life.</i>

01:44.820 --> 01:48.050
<i>He'll live if you feed</i>
<i>him mermaid flesh.</i>

01:49.360 --> 01:50.850
<i>Dad!</i>
<i>Dad!</i>

01:51.060 --> 01:52.320
<i>Don't shake him, Rin!</i>

01:55.460 --> 01:59.160
<i>He's all right. He won't die</i>
<i>from a scratch like this.</i>

01:59.870 --> 02:01.500
<i>I wonder.</i>

02:01.900 --> 02:04.300
<i>He looked pretty weak</i>
<i>from the illness.</i>

02:06.440 --> 02:08.500
<i>Isago!</i>

02:09.610 --> 02:11.200
<i>How dare you hurt my father!</i>

02:22.530 --> 02:23.750
<i>She's gone.</i>

02:26.960 --> 02:27.860
<i>Rin!</i>

02:28.100 --> 02:28.790
<i>Rin!</i>

02:29.230 --> 02:33.130
<i>Dad, don't die! I'll be right back</i>
<i>with mermaid flesh!</i>

02:34.900 --> 02:36.530
<i>Rin, wait!</i>

02:36.740 --> 02:38.010
<i>What's going on, Yuta?</i>

02:38.010 --> 02:39.110
<i>It's so late!</i>

02:39.110 --> 02:40.480
<i>Take care of the Chief!</i>

02:40.480 --> 02:41.700
<i>-What?</i>
<i>-The Chief?</i>

02:56.060 --> 02:59.150
<i>Mermaid, I'll find you</i>
<i>no matter what!</i>

03:06.580 --> 03:11.120
Episode 3
Village of the Fighting Fish
(Part II)

03:22.920 --> 03:24.890
They haven't made a move yet?

03:27.790 --> 03:29.120
Over there!

03:33.730 --> 03:36.660
Be careful! The current is
especially strong here!

03:42.170 --> 03:44.610
We'll run right into the
whirlpool if we go straight!

03:44.910 --> 03:46.400
Go around that island!

03:46.910 --> 03:48.100
They're going around the island!

03:49.410 --> 03:52.010
<i>Even we, the Sakagami Pirates,</i>
<i>couldn't read the tide...</i>

03:52.010 --> 03:55.140
<i>inside the territory</i>
<i>of Toba Island.</i>

03:55.580 --> 03:57.880
<i>But we've succeeded in</i>
<i>tricking them into guiding us!</i>

04:00.360 --> 04:01.950
Go!

04:18.940 --> 04:19.700
There it is!

04:25.750 --> 04:26.680
Mermaid!

04:28.180 --> 04:28.810
Yuta!

04:45.100 --> 04:48.700
<i>Don't run away from me, please!</i>
<i>Tell me, mermaid.</i>

04:50.410 --> 04:52.930
<i>How can I return to a
normal human being?</i>

05:05.960 --> 05:07.010
<i>What incredible strength!</i>

05:21.770 --> 05:22.460
Yuta!

05:29.750 --> 05:31.270
The Pirates of Sakagami?

05:44.460 --> 05:45.930
I can't believe it.

05:46.060 --> 05:48.330
This is what a mermaid looks like?

05:49.300 --> 05:51.930
The more I look at it,
the more disgusting it looks.

05:57.470 --> 05:58.300
It's come back to life.

05:58.740 --> 06:01.640
I see. It's not known as
the source of eternal youth...

06:01.640 --> 06:02.810
-and immortality for nothing.

06:02.810 --> 06:03.250
-And immortality for nothing.
-Help me!

06:03.250 --> 06:04.300
-Help me!

06:12.150 --> 06:13.180
Damn!

06:13.560 --> 06:16.620
Why are dead bodies so heavy?

06:32.470 --> 06:35.970
<i>There's no need to cry.</i>
<i>Yuta is going to come back to life.</i>

06:36.650 --> 06:42.410
Look at you,
you are a fully grown woman.

06:43.890 --> 06:45.910
A little, just a little bit.

06:46.120 --> 06:48.060
You bastard, what are you doing?

06:48.290 --> 06:51.520
What are you going to do
before your Chief's done with her?

06:51.990 --> 06:55.230
Well, hello, big sister.

07:02.040 --> 07:03.230
<i>Isago?</i>

07:04.310 --> 07:05.330
<i>How dare you hurt my father!</i>

07:07.480 --> 07:08.640
<i>How?</i>

07:10.150 --> 07:13.410
Get out of here!
I'm assigned to watch her here.

07:14.580 --> 07:15.680
Yes, ma'am.

07:16.320 --> 07:18.050
Excuse me, then.

07:23.290 --> 07:24.320
What is it?

07:24.930 --> 07:28.330
I thought I killed you.
But there's not even a scar.

07:29.930 --> 07:31.630
What's the matter?

07:32.000 --> 07:35.200
It's not as though you've never
seen an immortal before, is it?

07:36.270 --> 07:39.600
You ate mermaid flesh as well?

07:40.980 --> 07:43.600
Then why are you
looking for mermaid flesh?

07:44.350 --> 07:46.810
Even going so far as doing such an
awful thing to my father. Why?

07:54.360 --> 07:55.480
Right here.

07:56.390 --> 07:58.150
I have a baby in here.

07:58.630 --> 08:00.030
So what?

08:00.360 --> 08:03.130
I don't want to hear anything
about that brute's kid!

08:05.030 --> 08:07.400
It's a child from my former
husband who was murdered by...

08:07.840 --> 08:09.570
the Sakagami Pirates.

08:09.870 --> 08:11.610
Don't give me your lies!

08:11.610 --> 08:13.580
They say it's been three years
since you were kidnapped...

08:13.580 --> 08:15.270
and brought here!

08:16.710 --> 08:20.740
Three years. Yes.
I've waited for three long years.

08:21.350 --> 08:24.810
I need nourishment to
give birth to my baby.

08:25.650 --> 08:27.880
I need mermaid flesh.

08:29.360 --> 08:33.090
Well, I guess I'll go
have some fresh meat.

08:38.000 --> 08:41.230
Maybe the Chief's going to
keep all the meat to himself.

08:41.800 --> 08:43.830
Well, he just can't do that.

08:45.670 --> 08:48.200
Drag in Rin as entertainment
for the drinking party.

08:52.550 --> 08:54.520
Good work, Rin.

08:55.420 --> 08:58.720
Thanks to you,
I get to eat mermaid flesh.

09:05.390 --> 09:09.020
Damn. Why do I have to be
standing watch now, of all times?

09:15.770 --> 09:17.070
Where's Rin?

09:18.210 --> 09:20.840
You...I thought you died.

09:21.240 --> 09:24.410
Answer me quickly!
Or I'll crush your throat!

09:25.350 --> 09:27.370
At the fortress.

09:28.850 --> 09:30.840
Everyone, come out to the beach!

09:31.520 --> 09:33.580
Our Chief has managed
to come around.

09:34.320 --> 09:36.660
He says Isago of the
Sakagami Island attacked him.

09:37.460 --> 09:40.050
Then the one who stood
watch last night is also...

09:40.200 --> 09:40.890
Where's Miss Rin?

09:41.360 --> 09:43.330
Has she gone to Sakagami Island?

09:43.570 --> 09:45.120
Miss Rin...

09:48.640 --> 09:49.660
What's wrong, Rin?

09:50.240 --> 09:52.870
Can't you accept a
celebratory cup of sake from me?

09:58.010 --> 09:58.640
Rin.

10:00.880 --> 10:03.150
How dare can you kick my face?

10:06.890 --> 10:09.050
You're as spirited as always.

10:10.160 --> 10:11.630
Hey, what's the matter?

10:13.160 --> 10:15.560
You've got plenty of guts.

10:16.800 --> 10:18.330
It's a pity.

10:18.330 --> 10:22.930
If you were a little more sweeter,
I would've made you my wife, but...

10:25.540 --> 10:27.570
you're so ferocious, it's impossible!

10:33.250 --> 10:34.410
Yuta...

10:36.290 --> 10:38.010
Who the hell are you?

10:38.620 --> 10:40.590
I thought he died.

10:41.220 --> 10:43.560
I left too many things
left undone in this world...

10:43.690 --> 10:45.750
I had to come back to
life despite myself.

10:50.330 --> 10:53.170
There, there.
You're OK now.

10:54.670 --> 10:55.660
Yuta...

10:56.410 --> 10:58.970
"You're OK now"?
Screw you!

10:59.910 --> 11:02.810
Don't kid yourselves into thinking that
you'll be able to get out of here alive!

11:03.350 --> 11:05.810
He's an immortal who
ate mermaid flesh.

11:06.450 --> 11:09.280
If you want to kill him, you'll have
to sever his head or something.

11:14.120 --> 11:15.820
<i>Isago is immortal as well?</i>

11:16.760 --> 11:18.780
OK, that's interesting.

11:19.330 --> 11:22.590
I'll give mermaid flesh to whoever
takes off that guy's head.

11:23.470 --> 11:23.970
-It's mine!

11:23.970 --> 11:25.090
-It's mine!
-It's mine!

11:34.080 --> 11:34.910
Let's go.

11:34.910 --> 11:35.170
OK.

11:45.090 --> 11:46.820
I'm in pain.
Chief...

11:47.460 --> 11:50.910
Please, let me.
Let me have it!

11:52.830 --> 11:54.690
You idiot! You wouldn't deserve it
in a hundred years!

11:55.700 --> 11:58.170
It's a waste of time fighting
against drunken small-frys!

12:09.640 --> 12:12.080
Ouch.
That hurt!

12:16.790 --> 12:17.220
What?

12:21.590 --> 12:23.820
You! Who gave you the
permission to eat it?!

12:26.630 --> 12:28.290
We already ate it.

12:28.460 --> 12:30.560
Now we're immortal, too.

12:41.030 --> 12:50.950
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest

12:59.760 --> 13:01.730
Oh, my.
That's too bad.

13:02.130 --> 13:04.430
It seems the mermaid flesh
didn't go down too well with them.

13:05.230 --> 13:07.600
You said it was the elixir of
eternal youth and immortality.

13:07.900 --> 13:11.030
Too strong of any medicine
can become a poison.

13:13.410 --> 13:17.280
Only the luckiest become immortal.

13:19.580 --> 13:20.980
The rest die...

13:21.420 --> 13:23.380
or become monsters.

13:24.650 --> 13:25.480
It can't be.

13:27.260 --> 13:30.090
I see, it wouldn't be
interesting unless...

13:30.090 --> 13:32.960
There is a high stakes gamble
in order to obtain immortality.

13:39.070 --> 13:39.730
The wound!

13:40.270 --> 13:43.140
It seems that I have very good luck.

13:45.510 --> 13:49.770
Now it's an immortal against
an immortal. Let's settle this.

14:04.760 --> 14:06.060
Rin, go outside!

14:06.800 --> 14:08.520
I'm not leaving you here!

14:25.380 --> 14:26.280
Yuta!

14:28.820 --> 14:33.080
Well, now that he's quieted down,
I'll cut his head off with this.

14:35.920 --> 14:37.920
You didn't make it either.

14:38.330 --> 14:40.490
Isago, you...

14:42.460 --> 14:46.490
It's your fault.
You shouldn't have kidnapped me.

14:47.340 --> 14:50.360
There were many of my kind
from where I came from.

14:51.270 --> 14:56.010
There was no need to have
your men hunt for mermaids.

14:57.410 --> 14:59.970
You...what are you?

15:01.850 --> 15:03.680
I'm a mermaid.

15:06.960 --> 15:09.520
Yuta, wake up.
Wake up, Yuta!

15:09.520 --> 15:10.920
OK! OK!

15:21.470 --> 15:22.970
Take this!
And this!

15:22.970 --> 15:24.730
Why do they have to be so strong?

15:25.570 --> 15:26.800
Miss Rin!

15:28.540 --> 15:31.100
Miss Rin, are you all right?

15:33.350 --> 15:34.150
Guys!

15:34.150 --> 15:35.170
We're saved!

15:39.120 --> 15:42.950
You're a mermaid?

15:43.660 --> 15:45.390
You're joking.

15:45.960 --> 15:48.900
Some mermaids have legs.

15:49.730 --> 15:54.130
And the mermaids in sea
are our source of nutrition.

15:54.600 --> 15:56.090
"Our"?

15:57.870 --> 16:01.670
The nourishment I need
to give birth to my baby.

16:03.010 --> 16:04.980
I've waited for three long years.

16:06.180 --> 16:10.710
Sorry for pushing you over
a child that's not even yours.

16:12.090 --> 16:16.350
But I wanted to have
a baby at any cost.

16:28.340 --> 16:29.300
The Chief!

16:29.870 --> 16:31.000
Harpoon him!

16:40.250 --> 16:42.550
Shoot five or six into his back!

16:42.550 --> 16:43.380
OK!

16:48.290 --> 16:49.960
I don't care about anyone else...

16:49.960 --> 16:52.430
but you I have to kill.
For the good of the world!

17:05.140 --> 17:05.900
Isago?

17:18.420 --> 17:19.220
Isago!

17:19.390 --> 17:21.620
Why are you
running away to a cliff?

18:03.730 --> 18:06.740
Did she jump off because she
thought that she couldn't get away?

18:06.740 --> 18:08.790
But she was smiling.

18:09.400 --> 18:10.270
Yeah.

18:11.270 --> 18:12.710
She was smiling.

18:13.840 --> 18:15.170
Where did she go?

18:16.410 --> 18:17.400
I don't know.

18:50.780 --> 18:52.750
Has Yuta gone?

18:53.180 --> 18:53.940
Yeah.

18:54.520 --> 18:58.320
He said that he's simply
incapable of living here.

18:59.490 --> 19:03.790
<i>I hope you'll become</i>
<i>a normal human again.</i>

19:04.160 --> 19:09.190
<i>May a peaceful death</i>
<i>come upon you someday, Yuta.</i>

19:16.400 --> 19:19.860
<i>I can't live.</i>
<i>I only survive.</i>

19:26.380 --> 19:27.810
For a very short while...

19:29.280 --> 19:30.720
I had a nice dream.

19:35.620 --> 19:38.790
Was I in that dream of yours?

19:41.830 --> 19:42.760
Yeah.

19:43.330 --> 19:45.860
You were my wife.

20:01.650 --> 20:05.480
I had the same dream.

20:14.160 --> 20:15.190
Yuta.

20:15.760 --> 20:17.250
Live a long life.

20:19.200 --> 20:21.670
Don't be an idiot.
That's not a good omen.

20:47.100 --> 20:55.600
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

20:56.980 --> 21:05.490
ltsumade kakaruno to anata wa warau kedo
"How long does it take?" You smiled at me

21:06.950 --> 21:15.830
Dorekurai oboete iru hidoku naki nagara
How much do you remember? I cried hard

21:16.880 --> 21:26.390
Dorekurai oboete iru anokoto to ieba
How much do you remember if I talk about "that thing"?

21:31.470 --> 21:40.480
ltsumademo mada utsumuite
I still look down

21:41.440 --> 21:49.950
Tobikoe rarenai mizutamari
I can't jump over the puddle

21:51.080 --> 22:00.590
Wakaranakunaru moshikasuruto
I'm confused

22:00.920 --> 22:10.430
Kawarenai no wa watashi dake kana
Maybe I'm the only one who still can't change

22:15.390 --> 22:24.940
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

22:39.110 --> 22:40.100
What's the matter?

22:40.510 --> 22:42.870
You've been awfully
quiet for a long time.

22:43.480 --> 22:45.070
Oh, well...

22:49.780 --> 22:51.120
Are you bored?

22:59.190 --> 23:01.750
Do you want to give it a try?

23:16.210 --> 23:19.440
I didn't know waves were so heavy.

23:21.220 --> 23:25.120
Yeah, but you'll get used to it soon.

23:26.450 --> 23:28.180
How far do they continue?

23:29.320 --> 23:30.450
What?

23:34.060 --> 23:35.090
The waves.

23:37.300 --> 23:39.360
It looks like they
continue on forever.

23:40.470 --> 23:41.800
But there is an end.

23:43.340 --> 23:44.360
Let's hang in there.

23:49.210 --> 23:50.940
What's at the end?

23:55.180 --> 23:56.340
A port.

24:06.130 --> 24:07.860
Mana gets in a car accident.

24:08.130 --> 24:10.890
I rush to the clinic that
she gets taken to.

24:11.070 --> 24:14.520
But she's disappeared.
Where did she go?

24:15.100 --> 24:16.540
Looking everywhere for her...

24:16.540 --> 24:19.440
I reach a manor surrounded by
a forest with a mermaid legend.

24:19.740 --> 24:21.400
Two women live there.

24:21.980 --> 24:25.070
An old woman and a
young woman with snow-white hair.

24:26.180 --> 24:27.980
That dog is a Deformed One!

24:28.220 --> 24:29.480
Where's Mana?

24:29.990 --> 24:30.250
Episode 4
Mermaid Forest
(Part I)

24:30.250 --> 24:34.220
Episode 4
Mermaid Forest
(Part I)
Episode 4
"Mermaid Forest, Part I".

24:34.220 --> 24:34.980
Episode 4
Mermaid Forest
(Part I)
